    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0402" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 PW/1–1846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-18T17:00:00+03:00">January 18, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 18—1:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>173. ReDeptel 36, January 8. Note dated January 18 from Foreign Office states:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Soviet Govt has appointed to International Military Tribunal, in Tokyo
                            for the trial of the chief Jap war
                            criminals Director of Juridical <pb facs="0403" n="391" xml:id="pg391"/>
                            Sciences, Minister S. A. Golunsky as [associate] prosecutor for the
                            Soviet Union and Major General of Justice I. M. Zaryanov as a judicial
                            member of the military collegium of the supreme court of the
                                USSR.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d302-f1"/> They will depart with their
                            staff from Moscow for Tokyo in next few days.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d302-f1" n="99" xml:id="d302-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently garbled; Zaryanov was nominated as judge for the Tribunal.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
